001675                    ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
001676                    ; Building the map
001677                    ; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
001678                    
001679                    ; SDB_MAP_BUILD
001680                    ; Walks the FAT cluster chain of an open file once and stores the result as
001681                    ; an extent table, so that SDB_LBA can map blocks to LBAs afterwards. Costs
001682                    ; one SD card block read per 128 clusters of the file.
001683                    ;
001684                    ; Reads FAT sectors directly and therefore destroys the FAT32 library's
001685                    ; sector buffer, so it guards and restores it (see THE TWO RULES above). It
001686                    ; never modifies the file handle: the file position is the same afterwards.
001687                    ;
001688                    ; Input: R8: file handle (FDH)
001689                    ; R9: pointer to the block map to be filled
001690                    ; Output: none. The map is left invalid (extent count = 0, reason in
001691                    ; SDB_M_BAIL) when the file cannot be described, which makes all
001692                    ; callers fall back silently.
001693  8202  FF90  005E  SDB_MAP_BUILD               ASUB enter, 1
001694                    
